Navy aircraft . In 1961 , the Vinson Massif was named by the Advisory Committee on Antarctic Names ( US - ACAN ) , for Carl G. Vinson , United States congressman from the state of Georgia , for his support for Antarctic exploration . On Nov. 1 , 2006 , US - ACAN declared Mount Vinson and Vinson Massif to be separate entities . Mount Vinson is the highest peak in Antarctica , at 4,892 metres ( 16,050 ft ) . It lies in the north part of Vinson Massif 's summit plateau in the south portion of the main ridge of the Sentinel Range about 2 kilometres ( 1.2 mi ) north of Hollister Peak . It was first climbed in 1966 by an American team led by Nicholas Clinch . An expedition in 2001 was the first to climb via the Eastern route , and also took GPS measurements of the height of the peak . As of February 2010 , 1,400 climbers have attempted to reach the top of Mount Vinson .","entities":["Sentinel Range","Advisory Committee on Antarctic Names","Carl G. Vinson","Georgia","Antarctic exploration","Mount Vinson","Vinson Massif summit plateau","Hollister Peak","Naming of Vinson Massif","Declaration that Mount Vinson and Vinson Massif are separate entities","First climb of Mount Vinson","American team","Expedition","Eastern route","GPS measurements of the height of Mount Vinson"],"facts":["Sentinel Range -PART_OF-> Ellsworth Mountains","Vinson Massif & The Sentinel Range: New map -- new names -RELATED_TO-> Sentinel Range","C-130 Hercules -RELATED_TO-> Sentinel Range","flight into the Sentinel Range -RELATED_TO-> Sentinel Range","Carl Vinson -RELATED_TO-> Georgia"]}
