Legislative history Introduced in the Senate as S. 20 by Carl Levin ( D -- MI ) on January 25 , 1989 Passed the Senate on March 16 , 1989 ( 97 - 0 , Roll call vote 24 , via Senate.gov ) Passed the House on March 21 , 1989 ( Agreed voice vote ) Signed into law by President George H.W. Bush on April 10 , 1989 The Whistleblower Protection Act of 1989 , Pub. L. 101 - 12 as amended , is a United States federal law that protects federal whistleblowers who work for the government and report agency misconduct . A federal agency violates the Whistleblower Protection Act if agency authorities take ( or threaten to take ) retaliatory personnel action against any employee or applicant because of disclosure of information by that employee or applicant . Whistleblowers may file complaints that they believe reasonably evidences a violation of a law , rule or regulation ; gross mismanagement ; gross waste of funds ; an abuse of authority ; or a substantial and specific danger to public health or safety .","entities":["Whistleblower Protection Act of 1989","Carl Levin","Senate","House","George H.W. Bush","United States","Introduction of S. 20","Passage of the Whistleblower Protection Act by the Senate","Passage of the Whistleblower Protection Act by the House","Signing the Whistleblower Protection Act into law"],"facts":["Senate -PARTICIPATED_IN-> Carolyn Lerner's confirmation","Senate -RELATED_TO-> Whistleblower Protection Act","Passage of the Whistleblower Protection Act by the Senate -RELATED_TO-> Whistleblower Protection Act of 1989","Signing the Whistleblower Protection Act into law -RELATED_TO-> Whistleblower Protection Act of 1989","Passage of the Whistleblower Protection Act by the House -RELATED_TO-> Whistleblower Protection Act of 1989"]}
