{"Hawaii": "Hawaii", "connected_entity": "statehood", "connections": [{"fact": null, "type": "RELATED_TO", "relation": null}], "page": "Hawaii", "passage": "Hawaii\nmilitary personnel . Its capital is Honolulu on the island of Oʻahu . Hawaii is the 8th - smallest and the 11th - least populous , but the 13th-most densely populated of the 50 U.S. states . It is the only state with an Asian plurality . The state 's coastline is about 750 miles ( 1,210 km ) long , the fourth longest in the U.S. after the coastlines of Alaska , Florida , and California . Contents ( hide ) 1 Etymology 1.1 Spelling of state name 2 Geography and environment 2.1 Topography 2.2 Geology 2.3 Flora and fauna 2.4 Protected areas 2.5 Climate 3 History 3.1 First human settlement -- Ancient Hawai ʻi ( 800 -- 1778 ) 3.2 European arrival 3.3 Kingdom of Hawai ʻi 3.3. 1 House of Kamehameha 3.3."}
