The Sleeping Beauty ( ballet ) - wikipedia The Sleeping Beauty ( ballet ) Jump to : navigation , search Ballets by Pyotr Ilyich Tchaikovsky Swan Lake ( 1876 ) Sleeping Beauty ( 1889 ) The Nutcracker ( 1892 ) List of all compositions The Sleeping Beauty ( Russian : Спящая красавица / Spyashchaya krasavitsa ) is a ballet in a prologue and three acts , first performed in 1890 . The music was composed by Pyotr Ilyich Tchaikovsky ( his opus 66 ) . The score was completed in 1889 , and is the second of his three ballets . The original scenario was conceived by Ivan Vsevolozhsky , and is based on Charles Perrault 's La Belle au bois dormant . The choreographer of the original production was Marius Petipa . The premiere performance took place at the Mariinsky Theatre in St. Petersburg on January 15 , 1890 . The work has become one of the classical repertoire 's most famous ballets .","entities":["La Belle au bois dormant","Charles Perrault","Mariinsky Theatre","premiere performance","Russian","Ivan Vsevolozhsky","St. Petersburg","The Sleeping Beauty","Swan Lake","The Nutcracker","Marius Petipa","Pyotr Ilyich Tchaikovsky"],"facts":["Ivan Vsevolozhsky -RELATED_TO-> Tchaikovsky","Ivan Vsevolozhsky -WORKS_FOR-> Imperial Theatres","Charles Perrault -CREATED-> Sleeping Beauty","The Sleeping Beauty (ballet) -RELATED_TO-> Charles Perrault","Ivan Vsevolozhsky -PARTICIPATED_IN-> Petersburg production"]}
