1 Weekly charts 9.1. 2 Year - end charts 9.1. 3 Sales and certifications 9.2 Westlife version 9.3 Yuridia version 9.4 Parody versions 10 See also 11 References 12 External links Background and composition ( edit ) After her contract with RCA Records ended in 1981 , Tyler found a new manager in David Aspden and after seeing Meat Loaf perform `` Bat Out of Hell '' live on The Old Grey Whistle Test , approached Meat Loaf 's producer Jim Steinman and asked him to be her producer . Tyler visited Steinman in his apartment in New York in April 1982 with her manager , where she was presented with two tracks : `` Have You Ever Seen the Rain ? '' and `` Goin ' Through the Motions '' . She stated that had she not liked the songs Steinman played for her , he would have rejected Tyler 's invitation to collaborate . She returned to his studio apartment weeks later , where Steinman and Rory Dodd performed `` Total Eclipse of the Heart '' for her . He also hand - picked the recording band for the song .","entities":["Tyler","RCA Records","David Aspden","Meat Loaf","Bat Out of Hell","The Old Grey Whistle Test","Jim Steinman","Have You Ever Seen the Rain?","Goin' Through the Motions","New York","Rory Dodd","Westlife","Yuridia","Total Eclipse of the Heart"],"facts":["Tyler -RELATED_TO-> Spotify","Meat Loaf's a Hell raiser -RELATED_TO-> Meat Loaf","Tyler -RELATED_TO-> John Fogerty","Tyler -RELATED_TO-> The Times","Jim Steinman -CREATED-> Jim Steinman remix"]}

