{"song": "Joy to the World", "bandRelationship": "RELATED_TO", "band": "Three Dog Night", "writerRelationship": "CREATED", "songwriter": "Hoyt Axton", "source": "Joy to the World (Three Dog Night song)", "passage": "Joy to the World (Three Dog Night song)\nWhen the song hit number 1 on the US Billboard Hot 100 chart in 1971 , Axton and his mother , Mae Axton , became the first mother and son to each have written a number one pop single in the rock era . Mae Axton co-wrote `` Heartbreak Hotel '' , which was the first number one hit for Elvis Presley . In a 1994 case , David P. Jackson filed suit claiming co-authorship of the song and alleging that Axton fraudulently claimed sole authorship . In the suit Jackson claimed that Axton regularly credited him with co-authorship ."}
{"song": "Joy to the World", "bandRelationship": "RELATED_TO", "band": "Three Dog Night", "writerRelationship": "CREATED", "songwriter": "Hoyt Axton", "source": "Joy to the World (Three Dog Night song)", "passage": "Joy to the World (Three Dog Night song)\nIn the suit Jackson claimed that Axton regularly credited him with co-authorship . Charts and awards ( edit ) Weekly charts ( 1971 ) Peak position Australia KMR 8 Canadian Top Singles Germany ( Official German Charts ) 17 Netherlands ( Single Top 100 ) 25 New Zealand ( Listener ) 12 UK Singles ( Official Charts Company ) 24 US Billboard Hot 100 Year - end charts ( 1971 ) Rank Australia 50 Canadian Top Singles US Billboard Hot 100 The single had been out less than two months , when on April 9 , 1971 , `` Joy to the World '' was certified gold by the Recording Industry Association of America , for shipments of over 1,000,000 units across the United States . The record was also given a Gold Leaf award by RPM magazine for sales of over a million units . The record won the award for the Best Selling Hit Single Record by the National Association of Recording Merchandisers in March 1972 . It was also ranked by Billboard magazine as the year - end # 1 pop single of 1971 ."}
