This relationship ends when he has an affair with music major Martie Brodie ( played by Jane Adams ) while Lauren is out of town . After graduation , Alex accepts a job on Wall Street . Reception and influence ( edit ) Fox in September 1987 . The humor of the series focused on a real cultural divide during the 1980s , between the baby boomers and Generation X . According to Stephen Kiehl , this was when the `` Alex Keaton generation was rejecting the counterculture of the 1960s and embracing the wealth and power that came to define the ' 80s . '' While the youngest , Jennifer ( an athletic tomboy ) shares the values of her parents , Alex and Mallory embraced Reaganomics and consequent conservative values : Alex is a Young Republican and Mallory is a more traditional young woman in contrast to her feminist mother . In the Museum of Broadcast Communications entry for Family Ties , Michael Saenz argues that few shows better demonstrate the resonance between collectively held fictional imagination and what cultural critic Raymond Williams called `` the structure of feeling '' of a historical moment than Family Ties .","entities":["Jennifer","Alex P. Keaton","Martie Brodie","Jane Adams","Lauren","Wall Street","Fox","Family Ties","baby boomers","Generation X","Stephen Kiehl","counterculture","1960s","wealth and power","Mallory"],"facts":["Tina Yothers -RELATED_TO-> Jennifer","Jennifer -RELATED_TO-> Richard Nixon's presidential election","Alex P. Keaton -RELATED_TO-> Mallory Keaton","Alex P. Keaton -RELATED_TO-> Jennifer Keaton","Alex P. Keaton -RELATED_TO-> Andrew Keaton"]}
